      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand you feel stressed and want to alleviate the pressure quickly, but even with over-the-counter options like vitamin B and aspirin, it's essential to be cautious about self-medication. Vitamin B has many beneficial effects, and most people don't experience adverse side effects at typical dosages. However, such supplements can interact with other medications or underlying health issues you might have. Aspirin, especially in higher doses, can lead to stomach upset or even bleeding, which could be hazardous during a dizzy spell. I strongly recommend speaking with a pharmacist or healthcare provider to get personalized advice that considers your current health, even if it's now difficult fitting a doctor into your schedule. They can provide guidance on what medications might help or offer alternatives that could safely help you focus and alleviate your symptoms. Remember, turning to professionals, even under pressure, can help you avoid potential health risks in the long run.",
